blocks.text:
You become a part-owner of a real company. {{1}}
There is no real company with factories, employees and profits behind it. {{2}}
A dividend may be distributed if a profit is made. {{3}}
The price is determined by supply and demand in a marketplace. {{4}}
Fluctuations are often extreme – the price can jump by several tens of per cent within weeks. {{5}}
The value can fall – a loss is possible. {{6}}
You have voting rights at the general meeting. {{7}}
It is entirely digital money that works without a government, central bank or banks. {{8}}
In extreme cases, a total loss is possible. {{9}}
